    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0326" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg252"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Presidents Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-02">January 2,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum for the
                    President</hi>:</p>
                <p>Has Bullitt been answered relative to the French fleet, Alexandria?<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d136-f1"/></p>
                <p>You will recall that he, in effect, asked for instructions and I gather <pb
                        facs="0327" n="253" xml:id="pg253"/> that the joint view of the British and
                    ourselves is that Bullitt should not stir that up at the moment.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d136-f2"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry L. Hopkins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
